## Summary

Remove sheet-write latency from image search and thumbnail responses. Search reserves stable STOCK IDs and saves new rows asynchronously in batches of 20, deduplicating overlapping searches. Live thumbnail requests and background prefetch share Stock.Preview, the same library fetch function, and in-flight bytes; previews display immediately and persist afterward through the existing Stock.Keep/CONTENT path. Full-image downloads start immediately on selection, then import saves through the chosen STOCK row. Readiness is tracked per batch, and background saves participate in shutdown queue draining.

The initial change returned search results early but still delayed thumbnails until STOCK creation. Revised following the user's feedback to serve thumbnail bytes before persistence. Kept existing picker/import IDs and routes; pending reservations and preview bytes live in memory until their saves finish. Updated developer docs and removed the TODO item.

Database/image-search tests, focused race checks, access-layer checks, and go vet passed. Regression tests block commits while verifying thumbnails return and full-image downloads start, then verify import completion after release and earlier-batch readiness while later batches are blocked. No deployment or production latency measurement; completed imports still require saving the selected image through STOCK. Requested merge from main reported already up to date, with no conflicts.

